  "longBusinessSummary": "Vincorion SE develops and manufactures power and mechatronic solutions for defense platforms and aviation systems in Germany and internationally. The company develops and delivers integrated solutions that generate, manage, and store power for defense and civil protection operations. The company operates in three segments: Vehicle Systems, Power Systems, and Aviation. The Vehicle Systems segment develops and manufactures energy and stabilisation systems for military vehicles and support vehicles, including Leopard 2 main battle tank, the Puma infantry fighting vehicle, the Boxer armoured fighting vehicle and the PzH 2000 howitzer platforms, as well as selected applications for the rail sector. The Power Systems segment develops and delivers power supply systems for ground-based air defence systems and field-based missions, including gensets and integrated power supply systems for radars, firing, and command units used on platforms such as PATRIOT and IRIS-T, and tactical power systems for military equipment and critical infrastructure. The Aviation segment develops, manufactures, and delivers rescue hoists, heating systems, and other special products for military and civilian applications, such as hydraulic and electrical rescue hoists for helicopters, aircraft heating systems, and special aviation products, consist of radomes and aviation generators for military aircraft and surveillance systems. Vincorion SE was founded in 1895 and is based in Wedel, Germany.",
